---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../components/SectionHeader.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Why directories lie"
  description="Star averages, paid slots, and undated prices are costumes. A catalog is a git log or it is marketing."
>
  <SectionHeader
    title="Why directories lie"
    sub="Not a launch thread. The on-site case for a catalog you can audit — and against the ones you cannot."
  />

  <article class="max-w-2xl space-y-10 pb-16 text-[15px] leading-relaxed">
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[13px] font-bold tracking-[0.14em] text-ink uppercase">The costume</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink opacity-80">
        A 4.8 from eleven reviews is not a measurement. It is an invoice with a star on it. The
        sample is whoever clicked, the prompt is whoever paid for placement, and the number moves
        when the vendor does. Directories print it because a decimal looks like work.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink opacity-80">
        Noemium does not average vibes. The unit is a pull request: one YAML file, one named
        observer, one date, limitations printed next to the praise. Wrong? Edit the page. The
        history is public.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[13px] font-bold tracking-[0.14em] text-ink uppercase">Paid slots</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink opacity-80">
        “Featured” that you can buy is advertising with the lights off. Anchor cards on our floor
        are an editorial mix so the shelf is not only famous names — not a slot. Affiliate links
        exist, are declared in the file, and fail CI if they sneak into <span class="font-mono text-[13px]">url</span> or
        receipts undeclared. Every declined paid-influence offer is logged in the{' '}
        <a href="/refusals/" class="text-accent hover:underline">Open Refusal Ledger</a>. Today that
        ledger is zero. That is the honest count, not a branding flex.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[13px] font-bold tracking-[0.14em] text-ink uppercase">
        Prices without a date
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink opacity-80">
        An undated “from $19/mo” is a screenshot of a marketing page from whenever the intern last
        cared. We print a price only with a receipt, prefer the pricing page, and stamp
        last_verified. The trail on a tool page is git history of this repo — field changes we
        committed — not a live vendor ticker. If the number did not move in the changelog, we say
        so.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[13px] font-bold tracking-[0.14em] text-ink uppercase">
        No named skip
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink opacity-80">
        A directory that will not tell you when to walk away is selling the click-out. Limitations
        are required. Ship cards also carry a briefing — strengths, when to use, when to skip —
        all three or none. Ship is not a trophy. Status of that coverage is on{' '}
        <a href="/status/" class="text-accent hover:underline">/status</a>, rebuilt with the site,
        not scraped from vendors.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[13px] font-bold tracking-[0.14em] text-ink uppercase">
        What we print instead
      </h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 marker:font-mono marker:text-accent">
        <li>ship / situational / skip, with the job on the card</li>
        <li>receipts as footnotes, homepages marked as weak</li>
        <li>a date and a GitHub handle on every observation</li>
        <li>the file, the PR, the changelog — not a badge, not a vote, not a leaderboard</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[13px] font-bold tracking-[0.14em] text-ink uppercase">Catch us</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink opacity-80">
        Fork it. Break a number. Send the receipt.{' '}
        <a href="/contribute/" class="text-accent hover:underline">Contribute</a> is a PR queue, not
        a points program.{' '}
        <a href="/method/" class="text-accent hover:underline">Method</a> is how a card earns a
        verdict. If this page ever starts selling stars, paid slots, or a live price ticker, treat
        it as a regression and open the pull request.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
